The ported files below keep this copyright notice in their header comment and
say what was changed. No openFPGALoader binaries are distributed: the earlier
openFPGALoader WebUSB/WASM bundle (with LGPL libftdi1 and libusb linked in) was
removed when these TypeScript ports replaced it (#99).

Ported files:
- lib/jtag/gowin/fs.ts: from src/fsparser.cpp (Gowin .fs bitstream parser).
  Translated to TypeScript; errors are thrown instead of printed, and the
  header is returned as typed fields.
- lib/jtag/ftdi-mpsse.ts: from src/ftdiJtagMPSSE.cpp (FTDI MPSSE JTAG: Sipeed
  workarounds, TMS/TDI/TDO shifts, clock-only commands) and src/ftdipp_mpsse.cpp
  (MPSSE init, clock divisor, command buffering and reads).
  Translated to TypeScript over our USB transport instead of libftdi; the FTDI
  modem-status bytes are stripped here; the last bit of a shift is indexed by
  its absolute position, which fixes 9-bit shifts with `last`.
- lib/jtag/tap.ts: modelled on src/jtag.cpp (TAP reset and state moves, IR/DR
  shifts, scan-chain detection) and the Gowin READ_IDCODE opcode from
  src/gowin.cpp. Rewritten in TypeScript: state paths come from a search over
  the IEEE 1149.1 transition table, reads always drive TDI (a Sipeed firmware
  workaround), and results are plain-language verdicts.
- lib/jtag/gowin/gw2a.ts: from src/gowin.cpp (GW2A opcodes and status bits,
  send_command, readReg32, gw2a_force_state, enableCfg/disableCfg, pollFlag,
  eraseSRAM, writeSRAM, displayReadReg). Translated to TypeScript: polls stop
  after a time limit, failures return plain-language verdicts with a hint
  instead of printing, and progress goes to a callback. SRAM only.
- lib/jtag/gowin/gw2a-spi.ts: from src/gowin.cpp (Gowin::spi_put for the GW2A
  JTAG-to-SPI bridge, IR 0x16; prepare_flash_access, post_flash_access).
  Translated to TypeScript; the read path pads its extra byte with zeros.
- lib/jtag/spi-flash.ts: erase/program/verify order after src/spiFlash.cpp
  (SPIFlash::erase_and_prog). Rewritten in TypeScript over a generic SPI bus;
  writes are refused without an explicit confirmFlash.

